Short answer: there's no hosted product that does exactly this. The reliable path is a GitHub Actions cron that hits the API, writes JSON, and renders a static page. But the API gives you the right primitive for "authored only," so it's little work.

## The primitive that does the filtering for you

**GraphQL `contributionsCollection.commitContributionsByRepository`** — this is authored-commits-only by construction. Stars never appear (they live under a separate connection), and forks you merely bookmarked have zero commit contributions so they drop out automatically. Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/objects#contributionscollection

```graphql
query($login:String!, $from:DateTime!) {
  user(login:$login) {
    contributionsCollection(from:$from) {
      commitContributionsByRepository(maxRepositories:100) {
        repository { nameWithOwner url isFork isPrivate primaryLanguage { name } }
        contributions { totalCount }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Caveats worth knowing before you build on it: `from`/`to` must span ≤1 year, so you loop year by year; and commits only count if the author email is verified against the account (https://docs.github.com/en/account-and-profile/setting-up-and-managing-your-personal-account-on-github/managing-contribution-settings-on-your-profile/why-are-my-contributions-not-showing-up-on-my-profile).

## REST alternatives

- Own repos: `GET /users/{u}/repos?type=owner` then drop `fork === true` — https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#list-repositories-for-a-user
- Per-repo authored commits: `GET /repos/{o}/{r}/commits?author={u}` — https://docs.github.com/en/rest/commits/commits#list-commits
- Cross-repo: `GET /search/commits?q=author:{u}+sort:author-date` — https://docs.github.com/en/rest/search/search#search-commits (rate limit is 30/min authenticated; it also misses commits made under unlinked emails)
- Avoid `GET /users/{u}/events/public` as the backbone — capped at 300 events / 90 days: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/activity/events

## Existing projects you can crib or use directly

- **lowlighter/metrics** — https://github.com/lowlighter/metrics — renders SVG panels from your contribution data via Actions. Very close to what you want in spirit; note the repo is no longer actively developed, so treat it as reference more than dependency.
- **anuraghazra/github-readme-stats** — https://github.com/anuraghazra/github-readme-stats — hosted SVG cards; its `count_private`/commit-count logic is a useful read, though the default cards mix in stars.
- **OSS Insight** — https://ossinsight.io/ — query GitHub archive data, including per-user authored-commit breakdowns, without running your own crawler.
- **GH Archive** — https://www.gharchive.org/ — the raw event firehose, queryable from BigQuery, if you want a full historical log rather than API-window slices.

## Recommended shape

Actions workflow on a `schedule:` cron → GraphQL loop over years → write `data/commits.json` → commit it → static page renders from that file. The committed JSON is what makes the log genuinely static and diffable, and it survives API outages. `GITHUB_TOKEN` in Actions covers the auth; scheduled workflows on public repos are free.

Given you already have `data/` and a runner pattern in this repo, that fits the existing structure — say the word and I'll wire it up against your username.
